{"name":"Peeps","hex":"#ffcf38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Peeps","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of Peep"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Peeps"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peeps","blocks":[{"text":"Peeps are a marshmallow confection sold in the United States and Canada in the shape of chicks, bunnies, and other animals. They have been produced by candy maker Just Born since 1953. Peeps were the earlier creation of the R. E. Rodda Candy Company of Lancaster, PA, and were offered for sale as early as 1948."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Just_Born_Peeps_in_an_Easter_Basket.jpg/330px-Just_Born_Peeps_in_an_Easter_Basket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peeps","wikidata":"Q7160341"},{"title":"Peeps (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Peeps is a 2005 novel by Scott Westerfeld revolving around a parasite which causes people to become cannibalistic and repelled by that which they once loved. It follows the protagonist, Cal Thompson, as he lives with this parasite and tries to uncover a possible threat to the whole population of the world. The apocalyptic threat to the world that begins in Peeps continues in The Last Days, which features some of the same characters."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Westerfeld_-_Peeps_Coverart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peeps_(novel)","wikidata":"Q3552861"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Just_Born_building%2C_Bethlehem%2C_PA.jpg/500px-Just_Born_building%2C_Bethlehem%2C_PA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Just_Born_building%2C_Bethlehem%2C_PA.jpg/1280px-Just_Born_building%2C_Bethlehem%2C_PA.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki